      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c1e36f51",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts two police officers pointing at an unseen individual, with text that reads 'when cops see an unarmed black youth:' followed by the quote 'i want every gun we have to fire on that man.' This juxtaposition is designed to convey a hateful and racist message, implying that Black youth are inherently dangerous and deserving of lethal force, even when unarmed. It leverages a harmful stereotype that associates Black people with criminality and violence, and it promotes a dangerous narrative that justifies excessive use of force against Black individuals. The meme is explicitly hateful as it targets Black people based on their race and age, and it promotes a violent and racist worldview.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1a9e8813"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
